From 920d1987a736870b8947db629e2ce88f7fca7705 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matt C <latentcollapse@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 21 Sep 2026 06:20:16 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 01/45] Add neurabash as an additive code-execution tool
 alongside ipython

NIRA-Prime integration, first pass. Adds `neurabash` to the ToolName
registry as a second, separate tool - not a replacement for `ipython`.

Scope deliberately narrow: one-shot `--neura-profile=<profile> -c <code>`
per call (NeuraBash's ephemeral-session mode), no session persistence
across calls yet. ipython.ts's kernel remains the only path for RLM
sub-agent spawning, the Python skills bridge, file-edit diffs, and
attachments - NeuraBash has no equivalent for any of those yet, so
removing ipython would silently break them. Full scope and open
decisions are in the decision doc for Matt.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
